Looking at this problem, I need to understand the configuration: for each vertex, a circle outside the triangle is tangent to the opposite side and tangent to the circumcircle. I need to show concurrency of one set of cevians implies concurrency of the other.

**Key idea:** The tangency point $A_2$ on the circumcircle and the tangency point $A_1$ on side $BC$ are related by a homothety that reveals $A_1, A_2, M_A$ are collinear (where $M_A$ is the arc midpoint). This converts the problem into an equivalence of two Ceva conditions.

